      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If it feels like the nutrients are draining away too quickly, you might be dealing with leaching, which is often exacerbated by heavy watering or sandy soil. To combat this, you can try incorporating organic matter, like compost, into your soil. Compost acts like a sponge, holding onto those precious nutrients and releasing them slowly, which is much more sustainable than just constantly dumping fertilizer on the plants. This slow-release method is much better for long-term health.",
      "source": "target",
